@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### work logs (/worklog-api)
### add: ONLY the technician the ticket is assigned to (login as tech@sdp.test)
POST {{baseUrl}}/worklog-api/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Swapped the charger and tested the battery.",
  "minutesSpent": 25
}

### read: technician or manager of the ticket's team, or admin (response has totalMinutes)
GET {{baseUrl}}/worklog-api/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID

### --- negative cases ---

### minutesSpent must be a whole number from 1 to 1440 -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/worklog-api/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "bad minutes", "minutesSpent": 0 }

### a technician who is not assigned -> 404
### a manager or employee trying to add -> 403
### logging on a CLOSED / CANCELLED / REJECTED ticket -> 400
### the requester (employee) reading work logs -> 403
